{"title":"2022 SSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider an unfair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-sided die labeled from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, such that the probability of rolling a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is directly proportional to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c65360246ba03f500f3f327ea3fd1c9991db97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7-m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />. However, if we roll any number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then the probability of rolling a number less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the probability of rolling any number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive remains directly proportional to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c65360246ba03f500f3f327ea3fd1c9991db97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7-m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />. The expected number of rolls until a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is rolled can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693ffd9477da7b51b76b5c9f7b6073c00a19312a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" /> denote the expected number of rolls until a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is rolled given that the running minimum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. We work our way from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a55a8cc8e79af192d02d08500f9fd08d3605c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b08d5235f417c69f0cc0c2d473a4739abdb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, which is our answer. Clearly, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b9c019af4b8ec61baf3028166eb22e91aae6ac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_6=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fadb5585aed586f844891220d2428f59309d4401.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, we have \\begin{align*} E_5&amp;=\\frac{2}{3}(E_5+1)+\\frac{1}{3}(E_6+1)\\implies\\\\ E_5&amp;=\\frac{2}{3}E_5+1\\implies E_5=3. \\end{align*} For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a97996c8e5e403ffb2c283c5963ffba0c0222f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> we have \\begin{align*} E_4&amp;=\\frac{3}{6}(E_4+1)+\\frac{2}{6}(E_5+1)+\\frac{1}{6}(E_6+1)\\implies\\\\ 6E_4&amp;=3E_4+2E_5+E_6+6\\implies\\\\ 3E_4&amp;=2\\cdot3+0+6=12\\implies E_4=4. \\end{align*} For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165dd2fc3942a9bf6b44cfc4544eb8cfcad404ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, we have \\begin{align*} E_3&amp;=\\frac{4}{10}(E_3+1)+\\frac{3}{10}(E_4+1)+\\frac{2}{10}(E_5+1)+\\frac{1}{10}(E_6+1)\\implies\\\\ 10E_3&amp;=4E_3+3E_4+2E_5+E_6+10\\implies\\\\ 6E_3&amp;=3\\cdot4+2\\cdot3+0+10=28\\implies E_3=\\frac{14}{3}. \\end{align*} For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f263b4685391e1f4f3ba204a355cc203a29a0653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, we have \\begin{align*} E_2&amp;=\\frac{5}{15}(E_2+1)+\\frac{4}{15}(E_3+1)+\\frac{3}{15}(E_4+1)+\\frac{2}{15}(E_5+1)+\\frac{1}{15}(E_6+1)\\implies\\\\ 15E_2&amp;=5E_2+4E_3+3E_4+2E_5+E_6+15\\implies\\\\ 10E_2&amp;=4\\cdot\\frac{14}{3}+3\\cdot4+2\\cdot3+0+15=\\frac{155}{3}\\implies E_2=\\frac{31}{6}. \\end{align*} Finally, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b08d5235f417c69f0cc0c2d473a4739abdb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, we have \\begin{align*} E_1&amp;=\\frac{6}{21}(E_1+1)+\\frac{5}{21}(E_2+1)+\\frac{4}{21}(E_3+1)+\\frac{3}{21}(E_4+1)\\frac{2}{21}(E_5+1)+\\frac{1}{21}(E_6+1)\\implies\\\\ 21E_1&amp;=6E_1+5E_2+4E_3+3E_4+2E_5+E_6+21\\implies\\\\ 15E_1&amp;=5\\cdot\\frac{31}{6}+4\\cdot\\frac{14}{3}+3\\cdot4+2\\cdot3+0+21=\\frac{167}{2}\\implies\\\\ E_1&amp;=\\frac{167}{30}\\implies 167+30=\\boxed{197}. \\end{align*}\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018021946\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 123/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4825/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26196:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018021946 and revision id 280150. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}